{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(4,0,-3)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,5⟩=-11$, find the shortest distance from $P(-2,1,-1)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-34062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,0,-3⟩-⟨-2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-1,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨1,-4,5⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 5|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+4-10|}{\\sqrt{1+16+25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-34062" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7df4d0bc75c2dd3c24dfe3a8081d512f07aa13bb766e052b655e431b184d318"} {"question" "q-34062" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-34062" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{10\\sqrt{42}}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{11\\sqrt{42}}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\sqrt{42}}{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-34062" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,11,1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩=20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩ & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,9⟩-⟨-2,11,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-7,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨2,-5,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7df4d0bc75c2dd3c24dfe3a8081d512f07aa13bb766e052b655e431b184d318"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "55"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-6,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩=24.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩ & =24 \\\\ -8x+6y+3z & =24 \\\\ 3z & =24+8x-6y \\\\ z & =8+\\frac{8}{3}x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=3$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=8+\\frac{8}{3}(3)-2(1)=14.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(3,1,14)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,1,14⟩-⟨8,-6,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,7,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-8,6,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot (-8)+7\\cdot 6+9\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|40+42+27|}{\\sqrt{64+36+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|109|}{\\sqrt{109}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7df4d0bc75c2dd3c24dfe3a8081d512f07aa13bb766e052b655e431b184d318"} {"question" "q-80116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "\\sqrt{109}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-80116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{109}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(5,-1,9)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,-2⟩=3$, find the shortest distance from $P(7,-2,8)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,9⟩-⟨7,-2,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨3,-6,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6-6-2|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-14|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7df4d0bc75c2dd3c24dfe3a8081d512f07aa13bb766e052b655e431b184d318"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,2,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x+2y-4z=18.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2y-4z & =18 \\\\ 4(2)+2(1)-4z & =18 \\\\ -4z & =8 \\\\ z & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,1,-2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,1,-2⟩-⟨-7,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,2,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|9\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36-2+20|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|54|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{6} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a7df4d0bc75c2dd3c24dfe3a8081d512f07aa13bb766e052b655e431b184d318"} {"question" "q-129161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"} {"question" "q-129161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14076613/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e81d01fd13c15aa5bc29350cacad60178288a03beec48393375451ffcee6a81"}] "usage" {"q-34062" []} "basis" 2780 "retractions" [[17592186120228 :question/problem "Given that $Q(4, 0,-3)$ lies on the plane $Π: r \\cdot ⟨1,-4, 5⟩ =-11$, find the shortest distance from $P(-2, 1,-1)$ to $Π$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117869 17592186117870 17592186117871 17592186117872 17592186117873] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117868 :answer-field/